.TH Command SHIP REPORT
.SY "ship [<SHIP/FLEET> | <SECTS>]"
The ship report command is a census of your ships and lists all the
info available in readable format.
.s3
The <SHIP/FLEET> and <SECTS> arguments are provided in case you only
wish to look at one ship
or one fleet or all ships within a given area.
.s3
If no argument is given your entire navy will be listed.
.s3
The report format contains the following fields:
.s1
.in +1i
.L #
the ship number
.L type
the type of ship; "patrol boat", "submarine", etc,
.L x,y
the ship's current location (relative to your capitol),
.L f
the fleet designation letter (set by "create" command),
.L eff
the ship's efficiency,
.L civ
the number of civilians on board
.L mil
mil is the number of military on board
.L sh
the number of shells on board,
.L gun
the number of guns on board
.L pln
the number of planes on board
.L irn
the amount of iron on baord
.L dst
the amount of gold dust on board
.L gld
the number of gold bars on board
.L food
the amount of food on board
.L oil
the amount of oil on board
.L mu
the mobility of the ship
.in
.s1
For example:
.EX ship b
.NF
   #     type        x,y   f  eff civ mil  sh gun pln irn dst gld food oil mu
  10 patrol boat    -1,-3  b 100%   0  10   5   1   0   0   0   0   8   0   8
  18 oil derrick    -6,-4  b 100%  18   0   0   0   0   0   0   0  28 200 127
  22 fishing boat   -5,9   b 100%  10   0   0   0   0   0   0   0 100   0 127
  43 tender         -2,-4  b  83%   0  22   0  20   0   0   0   0  50  45  48
4 ships
.FI
.s3
